      "text": "The factor is the average of the two low-prior-return portfolios minus the average of the two high-prior-return portfolios, using the value-weighted 2x3 size/prior-return returns. Each month's value is `(SMALL LoPRIOR + BIG LoPRIOR)/2 - (SMALL HiPRIOR + BIG HiPRIOR)/2`. The script reads only the first (value-weighted monthly) block of the file, treats -99.99 and -999 as missing, and writes only months where all four required portfolios are available. I have not run it against the data.\n\n```python\nimport csv\nimport math\n\nINPUT = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_60_13.csv\"\nOUTPUT = \"output.csv\"\n\n\ndef is_missing(v):\n    return (abs(v + 99.99) < 1e-9) or (abs(v + 999.0) < 1e-9)\n\n\ndef parse_first_monthly_block(path):\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        for line in f:\n            s = line.strip()\n            if not s:\n                if started:\n                    break\n                continue\n            parts = [p.strip() for p in s.split(\",\")]\n            if len(parts) >= 7 and len(parts[0]) == 6 and parts[0].isdigit():\n                started = True\n                try:\n                    vals = []\n                    for x in parts[1:7]:\n                        v = float(x)\n                        vals.append(math.nan if is_missing(v) else v)\n                except ValueError:\n                    if started:\n                        break\n                    continue\n                rows.append((int(parts[0]), vals))\n            elif started:\n                break\n    return rows\n\n\ndef main():\n    rows = parse_first_monthly_block(INPUT)\n    out = []\n    for date, vals in rows:\n        # columns: 0 SMALL LoPRIOR, 1 ME1 PRIOR2, 2 SMALL HiPRIOR,\n        #          3 BIG LoPRIOR,   4 ME2 PRIOR2, 5 BIG HiPRIOR\n        sl, sh = vals[0], vals[2]\n        bl, bh = vals[3], vals[5]\n        needed = [sl, sh, bl, bh]\n        if any(math.isnan(x) for x in needed):\n            continue\n        lt_rev = (sl + bl) / 2.0 - (sh + bh) / 2.0\n        out.append((date, lt_rev))\n\n    with open(OUTPUT, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for date, val in out:\n            w.writerow([date, repr(float(val))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
